### Space Race JE widgets — the milestone panels, mounted on eight journal entries.
###
### Every milestone entry attaches two named roots from this file, in the UN's
### shape (un_layout_widget.gui):
###   custom_widget_container_1  widget_je_space_race_<m>_overview   the "?", then the overview
###   custom_widget_container_2  widget_je_space_race_<m>            the live sections
### The overview sits above the entry's one-line status text, the live sections
### below it. The waiting entry (je_space_race_interstellar_results) has no
### controls and no live sections: an overview only. Every explanation is on
### the Help page (te_space_race_help_popup, in gui/te_popups.gui), which the
### "?" at the top of each entry opens.
###
### Each section is a type (te_sr_sec_*); te_sr_status_sections sets their
### order, and te_sr_overview_milestone /
### te_sr_overview_transit compose the overview. What differs between
### milestones is only data (which scripted GUI the controls address, which
### script values and loc keys the panel reads), passed as sr_* blockoverrides
### by one pair of types per milestone (te_sr_<m>_overview, te_sr_<m>_status).
### The roots at the foot of this file wrap those, and the Timeline Extended
### window's Space Race tab (te_sr_tab_body, and its milestones' frames in
### gui/te_systems_window_generated.gui) instances the same
### types, so the two hosts draw one body. Vanilla ships several named widgets
### in one journal-entry widget file
### (gui/journal_entry_widgets/ep2_japan_widgets.gui:501,550 mounted by
### 00_meiji_restoration.txt:10,16).
###
### The panels replace the vanilla button grid, which is hidden from humans:
### every space race scripted button carries `is_ai = yes` in its `visible`, so
### the AI still picks its approach and funding through the buttons' ai_chance
### while a player sees only this. That makes the mapping an obligation — all
### four of the buttons' actions per milestone have a control here
### (te_sr_sec_control), and a fifth the grid never had:
###
###   op 0  Safe approach        op 2  funding −
###   op 1  Ambitious approach   op 3  funding +
###   op 4  Standard approach (player only; every milestone starts on it)
###
### The table is repeated in common/scripted_guis/space_race_sguis.txt; keep the
### two in step. Neither side holds a rule: every op delegates to the shared
### sr_possible_* trigger and sr_effect_* effect that the journal-entry buttons
### call, so the grid and the panel cannot drift.
###
### DATA CONTRACT — everything shown comes from script, nothing is re-derived:
###   state (status cell) -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_status_<m>'), read from
###                          sr_<m>_last_status, whose single derivation site
###                          is sr_set_milestone_status_base; its tooltip is the
###                          matching sr_pace_note_* sentence, and Safe and
###                          Ambitious carry their weekly cost in the word
###                          (sr_disp_cost_*_<m>)
###   progress / goal     -> ScriptValue('sr_progress_<m>_value'), ('sr_<m>_goal');
###                          the bar reads sr_disp_progress_frac_<m>, the same
###                          two numbers as a 0..1 fraction
###   pace                -> ScriptValue('sr_pace_rate_<m>'), the rate the pulse
###                          actually applies
###   setback risk        -> ScriptValue('sr_risk_shown_<m>'), the value the roll
###                          uses
###   the first           -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_first_claimed_<m>')
###   setbacks, estimate  -> sr_setbacks_<m>_value, sr_eta_months_<m>
###   mission profile     -> GetCustom('sr_<m>_profile')
###   reward preview      -> GetStaticModifier('sr_first_<m>').GetDesc in the
###                          progress bar's tooltip, never a typed number
###   who else is racing  -> estimate rows, a datamodel of the viewer's list
###                          sr_rivals_list_<m> (each rival's capital, furthest
###                          first, from sr_rivals_estimate_refresh; items
###                          Scope.GetState, the country through
###                          State.GetCountry: gotchas #11, #15), the numbers
###                          from sr_disp_rival_{est,lo,hi}_<m> with the rival
###                          passed in (AddScope 'sr_rival'); the rows' hovers
###                          read GetPlayer, as an item's tooltip has no
###                          JournalEntry (gotcha #24)
###   our colonies        -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_colony_<world>_<specialization>')
###                          and ('sr_disp_colonies_held'),
###                          from each <modifier>_held record; solar colonization's
###                          te_sr_sec_colonies section only. A row's tooltip is
###                          GetStaticModifier(<modifier>).GetDesc in its loc key.
###   a colony's window   -> te_sr_colony_popup (the owner, 2026-11-23), in
###                          te_popups: a colony's page (te_sr_colony_page)
###                          with every colony we hold listed beside it, opened
###                          by a colony's name, its row in Solar System or its
###                          marker on the map (te_popup = sr_colony,
###                          sr_colony_focus the colony's key; client-side);
###                          the page's blocks are the list row's, filled again
###   a fleet's window    -> te_sr_fleet_popup (the owner, 2026-11-25), in
###                          te_popups: a fleet's page (te_sr_fleet_page) with
###                          every fleet we have listed beside it, opened by
###                          the arrow at the head of its card (sr_fleet_focus
###                          the slot; client-side, and the window's own key,
###                          so the pickers its orders open on te_popup draw
###                          over it and come back to it); the page's blocks
###                          are the card's, filled again, and its fire is
###                          sr_disp_fl_<n>_fire_fleets and _fire_defences
###   the system map      -> te_sr_system_map (the owner, 2026-11-23), at the
###                          head of Solar System: each site's marker reads
###                          sr_disp_site_<key>, _target_<key> and
###                          _inbound_<key>, the values its row in the list
###                          reads; a location picked there (sr_ss_loc,
###                          client-side) lists that location's sites alone
###   programme row       -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_<m>'); each icon's
###                          tooltip is GetCustom('sr_prog_<m>'). The
###                          interstellar icon's four states read
###                          sr_disp_prog_interstellar
### The sr_disp_* values are in common/script_values/space_race_display_values.txt.
###
### The Timeline Extended window's Space Race tab also has two sections of its
### own (te_sr_sec_powers, te_sr_sec_orbit), which read no journal entry and so
### show between milestones; neither is mounted in the journal. The tab draws
### them after the milestones' blocks (owner, 2026-10-27), and Orbit carries the
### debris row the journal's Mission Control has, so the tab's milestone
### instances override "sr_debris" empty:
###   space powers        -> our row on GetPlayer.GetCapital; the others a
###                          datamodel of the viewer's list sr_powers_list (each
###                          power's capital, furthest along first, from
###                          sr_powers_refresh; sr_power_total says whether it
###                          has run yet); each icon reads
###                          sr_disp_prog_<m> on the row's power, its hover
###                          GetCustom('sr_power_prog_<m>'); the estimate is the
###                          Rivals rows' band (sr_disp_rival_{lo,hi}_<m>) for
###                          the code sr_disp_power_lead picks, ours exact
###                          (sr_disp_progress_frac_<m>)
###   orbit               -> the debris row; te_asat_disp_* and the custom loc
###                          te_asat_satellites_state / te_asat_moratorium_state
###                          (common/script_values/te_orbital_debris_values.txt,
###                          te_orbital_debris_custom_loc.txt); the strike's
###                          checklist and targets from te_asat_strike_ready_sgui,
###                          the last strike from te_asat_record_sgui
###
### COST. The Rivals rows read a stored list and evaluate three small script
### values each per frame. The monthly refresh that fills the list runs for
### players only. Space Powers works the same way (sr_powers_refresh); its
### rows evaluate a code and their icons' small values per frame, while the
### tab shows them.
###
### Widths are fixed, never content-sized: every root and composer is 520
### wide (`minimumsize`), each panel's content 480, and rows of numbers use
### fixed columns, so nothing shifts when a value changes length.
###
### Every root is gated on `[JournalEntry.IsActive]`: all eight entries carry
### `is_shown_when_inactive`, so a widget is otherwise built for countries that
### hold none of the space race's variables — the failure mode that produced
### ~1,000 "Failed to fetch variable" errors on the UN chamber's first in-game
### test (docs/guides/gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #14).
###
### Collapse flags say their default (test_space_race_layout.py): *_closed
### sections are open until closed, *_open ones collapsed until opened. The live
### sections' flags are per milestone (`sr_panel_control_<m>_closed`,
### `sr_panel_rivals_<m>_closed`), because several milestone entries can be
### active at once. They live in GetVariableSystem, which is client-side,
### never saved and invisible to script.

### TYPE SIZES (style guide rule 3, the owner 2026-10-17; audit SPC-11): rows,
### values, buttons and notes 17, subheadings 20, the overview 16 in the
### tooltip face, each through these templates, so a pass on type edits three
### numbers. test_space_race_labels.py reads them and holds every fixed cell to
### its longest text at these sizes.
template te_sr_fontsize_row {
	fontsize = 17
}

template te_sr_fontsize_heading {
	fontsize = 20
}

template te_sr_fontsize_overview {
	fontsize = 16
	using = tooltip_font
}

types space_race_widget_types
{
	### ======================================================================
	### PRIMITIVES (shapes copied from un_chamber_widget.gui)
	### ======================================================================
	type te_sr_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_sr_fontsize_row
	}

	type te_sr_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2
		margin = { 20 8 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type te_sr_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, with a faint rule under it
	### (un_chamber_subheader).
	type te_sr_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_heading
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading (un_chamber_note). Static keys only.
	type te_sr_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_sr_fontsize_row
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left and its value on the right
	### (un_chamber_value_row), the value column wide enough for the longest
	### figure, an estimate of "1300 months". A row's tooltip opens its
	### breakdown; nothing is underlined (style guide rule 3, as vanilla).
	type te_sr_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 330 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 330 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_row
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 130 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 130 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#v"
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### One approach option. `action_binding` carries the four properties that
	### address the scripted GUI, because they are the only part that differs
	### between the three options; the sizing is shared (110 + 3 × 116 + 3 × 4
	### fits the 480 content width).
	type te_sr_action_button = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 116 30 }
		parentanchor = vcenter

		textbox = {
			parentanchor = center
			align = center|nobaseline
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 106
			elide = right
			using = te_sr_fontsize_row
			block "action_label" {}
		}

		block "action_binding" {}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW PIECES
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview's first row: an icon, its word small beneath
	### (te_un_ov_icon_label). Fixed width, so the row cannot push the panel
	### wider: three cells fill the 480 column (3 × 156 + 2 × 6). At the
	### overview's 16 points (audit SPC-11) the word may take two lines: Safe and
	### Ambitious carry their weekly cost under the word ("Ambitious" /
	### "−360 a week"), so the cell is 78 high and the word sits under the icon
	### (round 3; test_space_race_labels.py holds every line to its cell).
	### `icon_alpha` dims the icon.
	type te_sr_ov_icon_label = widget {
		size = { 156 78 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			block "icon_alpha" {}
			block "icon_texture" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 38 }
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 154 -1 }
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### "The first": open (lit) or claimed by another power (dimmed). The
	### instance sets which one shows; the tooltips are the sentences the
	### Rivals list used to open with.
	type te_sr_ov_first = flowcontainer {
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
			block "first_open" {}
			tooltip = "sr_rivals_first_open"
			blockoverride "icon_texture" {
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first.dds"
			}
			blockoverride "label" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_first_open"
			}
		}
		te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
			block "first_claimed" {}
			tooltip = "sr_rivals_first_claimed"
			blockoverride "icon_alpha" {
				alpha = 0.25
			}
			blockoverride "icon_texture" {
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first.dds"
			}
			blockoverride "label" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_first_claimed"
			}
		}
	}

	### Progress towards the goal: a label, the bar and the headline
	### ("124 / 200 (+3.5/mo)"); the tooltip is on the whole row, as the UN's
	### authority row. The bar ends at the goal, so it needs no target marker.
	### Fixed columns (110 + 140 + 210, with the spacing 476), so a longer number
	### never moves the bar. The label column fits the longest label, "Next
	### Colony"; the headline column the longest figure, "650 / 650 (+99.9/mo)"
	### (round 3: "Next Colony" was cut to "Next Colo..." at 90). The tooltip's
	### block is "row_tooltip", not "bar_tooltip": that name is the history
	### charts', whose bar tooltips have no JournalEntry to read
	### (test_history_chart_tooltip_context.py).
	type te_sr_ov_bar_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		spacing = 8
		parentanchor = hcenter
		block "row_tooltip" {}

		textbox = {
			minimumsize = { 110 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 110 -1 }
			autoresize = yes
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "bar_label" {}
		}
		default_progressbar_horizontal = {
			size = { 140 18 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			blockoverride "values" {
				block "bar_value" {}
				min = 0
				max = 1
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 210 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 210 -1 }
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "bar_text" {}
		}
	}

	### Another country's progress on a milestone (National Info, spec
	### 2026-11-02-charts-help-national-info § 6.4), in the exact bar's place:
	### the Rivals rows' estimate band and marker (sr_disp_rival_lo/hi/est_<m>),
	### with the country as its own viewer and rival, so the band is the open
	### one, a quarter of the goal either side, around the marker its yearly
	### offset places (sr_fuzz_<m>). te_sr_ov_bar_row's layout (110 + 140 + 210
	### and two gaps of 8), so the row keeps the bar's width. The instance passes
	### the label, the three values and the text.
	type te_sr_ov_band_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		spacing = 8
		parentanchor = hcenter
		tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_band_tt"

		textbox = {
			minimumsize = { 110 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 110 -1 }
			autoresize = yes
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "band_label" {}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 140 18 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			white_progressbar_horizontal = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				blockoverride "values" {
					block "band_hi" {}
					min = 0
					max = 1
				}
			}
			default_progressbar_horizontal = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				blockoverride "background" {}
				blockoverride "frame" {}
				blockoverride "values" {
					block "band_lo" {}
					min = 0
					max = 1
				}
				blockoverride "on_top_of_the_progressbar" {
					progressbar = {
						noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
						progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
						size = { 100% 100% }
						skip_initial_animation = yes
						direction = horizontal
						block "band_est" {}
						min = 0
						max = 1
						marker = {
							icon = {
								size = { 24 18 }
								parentanchor = vcenter
								widgetanchor = center
								texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 210 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 210 -1 }
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "band_text" {}
		}
	}

	### A share of the 40 worlds as a framed pie (te_un_ov_pie, with a third
	### layer): the disc is the unclaimed rest, then every world claimed, then
	### ours on top — largest first (gui_modding_guide.md, "Pie charts of
	### script-held data"). The textures: docs/systems/space_race_gui_icons.md.
	type te_sr_ov_pie = widget {
		size = { 150 108 }

		icon = {
			size = { 86 86 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 62 62 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 12 }

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_unclaimed.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_claimed" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_claimed.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_ours" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_ours.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			block "pie_label" {}
		}
	}

	### One entry of the programme row: its journal icon (PR #571) at full
	### colour once achieved, half while under way, faint otherwise, with a
	### flag in the corner when we were first. The instance sets the texture
	### on the three icons and the code tests that pick one.
	type te_sr_ov_prog_cell = widget {
		size = { 50 50 }

		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			block "lit" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.6
			block "running" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.25
			block "unlit" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 18 18 }
			parentanchor = top|right
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first_mark.dds"
			block "first" {
				visible = no
			}
		}
	}

	### The Interstellar Probe and the wait for its data, one cell with four
	### states (owner's play-test, round 3). Each state is its own icon, with
	### its own texture and hover, shown by one equality test on
	### sr_disp_prog_interstellar, so no two can show at once: 0 not begun,
	### 1 under way, 2 launched and awaiting data, 3 data received. Each
	### state's art (PR #586, space_race_gui_icons.md) carries the state, so
	### none is faded. The flag marks a first, as in te_sr_ov_prog_cell, and
	### lets the hover through to the state beneath it.
	type te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar = widget {
		size = { 50 50 }

		### 0: not begun, or another power finished it first
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_not_begun.dds"
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_0', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_0_ni' )]"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
		}

		### 1: under way
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_under_way.dds"
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_1', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_1_ni' )]"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
		}

		### 2: launched, awaiting data
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_awaiting_data.dds"
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_2', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_2_ni' )]"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
		}

		### 3: data received
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_data_received.dds"
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_3', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_3_ni' )]"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
		}

		icon = {
			size = { 18 18 }
			parentanchor = top|right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first_mark.dds"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
		}
	}

	### The whole programme, eight icons in a row under a centred label: the
	### same on every panel. Each icon's tooltip is the row of the old
	### "programme so far" list (name and state, sr_prog_<m>). The Interstellar
	### Probe and its wait for data share the seventh icon, which has four
	### states of its own (te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar). Code order:
	### space_race_display_values.txt, sr_disp_prog_*.
	type te_sr_ov_programme = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		spacing = 2
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			parentanchor = hcenter
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_sr_fontsize_overview
			text = "je_space_race_widget_programme_header"
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_ov_programme_tt', 'je_space_race_widget_ov_programme_tt_ni' )]"
		}
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 3
			parentanchor = hcenter

			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_suborbital', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_suborbital_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_suborbital.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_orbital', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_orbital_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_orbital.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_landing', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_landing_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_moon_landing.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_probe', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_probe_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_probe.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_base', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_base_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_moon_base.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_prog_mars_landing', 'je_space_race_widget_prog_mars_landing_ni' )]"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_mars_landing.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar = {}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_solar_colonization"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_solar_colonization.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW COMPOSERS
	### ======================================================================

	### The overview of a milestone with controls (seven entries). Row 1: the
	### state, the setback risk, and "the first" (or, for colonization, the
	### stage); row 2: progress; then any extra rows (colonization's worlds
	### pie); then the programme. The datacontext is the milestone's scripted
	### GUI, set on the root. While it is not shown (solar colonization held
	### open for its colony modifiers, or its production method switched off),
	### the state reads Idle and the risk and progress rows are hidden.
	type te_sr_overview_milestone = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 520 -1 }
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_window_space_race_tab_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"

		te_sr_panel = {
			spacing = 10

			### Row 1, in two rows with fixed contents, each with its own visible:
			### running, the state, the setback risk and the third cell (480);
			### idle, Idle beside the third cell (318). One row that was 318 idle
			### and 480 running was centred at the width it was first drawn, so a
			### programme resumed with the panel open ran it to about 561, past the
			### 480 column (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #43). The third cell is a
			### block in both rows, and one blockoverride fills both.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 6
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"

				### The state: one of three cells shows. The approach is the
				### player's own (National Info shows another country the third
				### cell alone).
				flowcontainer = {
					using = te_own_country_only
					ignoreinvisible = yes

					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_standard" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_standard"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_standard.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_standard_label"
						}
					}
					### Safe and Ambitious carry their weekly cost in the word
					### (round 2: "make that clear").
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_safe" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_safe"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_safe.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_label_safe" {}
						}
					}
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_ambitious" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_ambitious"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_ambitious.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_label_ambitious" {}
						}
					}
				}

				### Setback risk: lit while the monthly roll is made, faint at 0%
				### (no longer reached: the risk is at least 1% since the cooldown went).
				### The player's own, as the approach is.
				flowcontainer = {
					using = te_own_country_only
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_risk_tt"

					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_risk_lit" {}
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/risk.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_risk_label" {}
						}
					}
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_risk_unlit" {}
						blockoverride "icon_alpha" {
							alpha = 0.25
						}
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/risk.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_risk_label" {}
						}
					}
				}

				### The first (seven milestones) or the stage (colonization).
				block "sr_third_cells" {}
			}

			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 6
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) )]"

				### The state while the programme isn't running.
				te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
					tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, 'je_space_race_widget_ov_idle_tt', 'je_space_race_widget_ov_idle_tt_ni' )]"
					blockoverride "icon_texture" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_idle.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_idle"
					}
				}

				### The first (seven milestones) or the stage (colonization).
				block "sr_third_cells" {}
			}

			### Row 2: progress, while the programme runs. The player's own
			### country sees the exact bar; another country (National Info, spec
			### 2026-11-02-charts-help-national-info § 6.4) the estimate band in
			### its place, at the bar's width, so the row is one of the two
			### whenever it shows.
			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				direction = vertical
				parentanchor = hcenter
				ignoreinvisible = yes

				te_sr_ov_bar_row = {
					using = te_own_country_only
					blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
						block "sr_progress_tooltip" {}
					}
					blockoverride "bar_label" {
						block "sr_progress_label" {}
					}
					blockoverride "bar_value" {
						block "sr_progress_value" {}
					}
					### The headline's rate opens the breakdown of where the pace
					### comes from; the rest of the row keeps the reward preview.
					blockoverride "bar_text" {
						tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_pace_tt"
						block "sr_progress_text" {}
					}
				}
				te_sr_ov_band_row = {
					visible = "[Not( Country.IsLocalPlayer )]"
					blockoverride "band_label" {
						block "sr_progress_label" {}
					}
					blockoverride "band_lo" {
						block "sr_band_lo" {}
					}
					blockoverride "band_hi" {
						block "sr_band_hi" {}
					}
					blockoverride "band_est" {
						block "sr_band_est" {}
					}
					blockoverride "band_text" {
						block "sr_band_text" {}
					}
				}
			}

			block "sr_extra_rows" {}

			te_sr_ov_programme = {}
		}
	}

	### The waiting entry's overview: the transit and the programme.
	type te_sr_overview_transit = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 520 -1 }
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_window_space_race_tab_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"

		te_sr_panel = {
			spacing = 10

			te_sr_ov_bar_row = {
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_transit_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_transit_label"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_value" {
					value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_progress_frac_interstellar_results') )]"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_progress_interstellar_results"
				}
			}

			te_sr_ov_programme = {}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### LIVE SECTIONS (open by default)
	### ======================================================================

	### Mission Control: the approach selector and the funding stepper, the
	### figures they move, and the mission profile.
	###
	### The controls, the setbacks and the estimate are gated on the scripted
	### GUI's is_shown, which is the same gate the milestone's four
	### journal-entry buttons use. That is what keeps the funding cell's `Var`
	### read safe, and what hides them when solar colonization drops into
	### passive mode with every colony claimed or its method off; the estimate
	### would otherwise quote a pace nothing is adding.
	type te_sr_sec_control = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2

		te_sr_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_control_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				block "control_onclick" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				block "control_showmore" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				block "control_showless" {}
			}
		}

		te_sr_panel = {
			block "control_visible" {}

			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				spacing = 4
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"

				### Approach — ops 4 (Standard), 0 (Safe) and 1 (Ambitious),
				### beside their label. The option already in force greys itself
				### out through is_valid, and its tooltip says so (IsValidTooltip,
				### then what it does and what it costs a week). The two rows are
				### left-aligned so their labels form one column.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 4
					ignoreinvisible = yes

					textbox = {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_approach_label"
						size = { 110 30 }
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_standard_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_safe_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_ambitious_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}
				}

				### Funding — op 2 down, op 3 up, beside their label. The ceiling
				### is sr_max_funding_level_soft, six levels past the cap, read by
				### the shared trigger the plus button asks (lunar colonization
				### design § 5.1). Past the cap the figure reads "9 / 7 (+0.8)":
				### the level, the cap, and the effective levels the excess adds,
				### so the cell is wide enough for "28 / 22 (+1.6)".
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 4
					ignoreinvisible = yes

					textbox = {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_funding_label"
						size = { 110 26 }
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					button_icon_minus_action = {
						size = { 26 26 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ) ) )]"
					}

					textbox = {
						block "funding_value" {}
						size = { 140 26 }
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					button_icon_plus_action = {
						size = { 26 26 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ) ) )]"
					}
				}
			}

			### The figures pace and risk leave out (both are in the overview).
			te_sr_value_row = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_setbacks_label"
				}
				blockoverride "row_value" {
					block "setbacks_value" {}
				}
			}
			te_sr_value_row = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_eta_tt"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_eta_label"
				}
				blockoverride "row_value" {
					block "eta_value" {}
				}
			}

			### Orbital debris, for every milestone (te_orbital_debris_widget.gui).
			### The Space Race tab shows it once, in Orbit: its milestone
			### instances override "sr_debris" empty (passed down as
			### control_debris and status_debris).
			block "control_debris" {
				te_sr_debris_row = {}
			}

			### Milestone-specific rows: solar colonization's Next Windows
			### (te_sr_sec_windows, gui/sr_launch_window_widgets.gui).
			block "control_extra" {}

			### The mission profile. Its heading keeps its top margin only
			### when the controls are above it, so the section never opens on
			### an empty line.
			te_sr_subheader = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_profile_header"
				}
			}
			te_sr_subheader = {
				visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) )]"
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_profile_header"
				}
			}
			te_sr_text = {
				block "profile_text" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### One rival in the Rivals section: its name, its estimated progress as a
	### band with a marker, and the band in words; the tooltip says it is an
	### estimate and what narrows it. The name has the whole 480 line to
	### itself, because a country's name can run to 48 characters ("United
	### Socialist Council Republics of California"), which no column beside a
	### bar holds without "..." (round 3; test_space_race_labels.py). The bar
	### and the band in words share the line beneath, in fixed columns
	### (380 + 92, with the spacing 480), so nothing shifts as the numbers move.
	### An item of the Rivals datamodel (te_sr_sec_rivals): the rival's capital
	### is the item's datacontext, and the hover reads GetPlayer, since an
	### item's tooltip loses JournalEntry (gotcha #24).
	###
	### The bar is two layers and a marker: a white bar to the top of the band,
	### the plain bar to its bottom over it (its own background and frame
	### blanked, as the UN tally's upper layers do), and the marker at the
	### estimate (the marker technique of the UN's authority bar).
	type te_sr_rival_row = widget {
		size = { 480 42 }

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			spacing = 2
			block "row_tooltip" {}

			textbox = {
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
				autoresize = yes
				elide = right
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_sr_fontsize_row
				text = "je_space_race_widget_rival_name"
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 8
				widget = {
					size = { 380 14 }
					parentanchor = vcenter

					white_progressbar_horizontal = {
						size = { 100% 100% }
						blockoverride "values" {
							block "row_hi" {}
							min = 0
							max = 1
						}
					}
					default_progressbar_horizontal = {
						size = { 100% 100% }
						blockoverride "background" {}
						blockoverride "frame" {}
						blockoverride "values" {
							block "row_lo" {}
							min = 0
							max = 1
						}
						blockoverride "on_top_of_the_progressbar" {
							progressbar = {
								noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
								progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
								size = { 100% 100% }
								skip_initial_animation = yes
								direction = horizontal
								block "row_est" {}
								min = 0
								max = 1
								marker = {
									icon = {
										size = { 24 18 }
										parentanchor = vcenter
										widgetanchor = center
										texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
				textbox = {
					minimumsize = { 92 -1 }
					maximumsize = { 92 -1 }
					autoresize = yes
					elide = right
					parentanchor = vcenter
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_sr_fontsize_row
					block "row_range" {}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Rivals: every other power whose program is running this milestone and
	### moving, each an estimate row (te_sr_rival_row), furthest first: a
	### datamodel of the viewer's list sr_rivals_list_<m>, the rivals'
	### capitals (sr_rivals_estimate_refresh, space_race_effects.txt; audit
	### SPC-9). Whether "the first" is still open is the overview's.
	type te_sr_sec_rivals = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2

		te_sr_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_rivals_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				block "rivals_onclick" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				block "rivals_showmore" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				block "rivals_showless" {}
			}
		}

		te_sr_panel = {
			block "rivals_visible" {}

			te_sr_text = {
				block "rivals_none" {}
				text = "sr_rivals_none"
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 2
				block "rivals_datamodel" {}

				item = {
					te_sr_rival_row = {
						datacontext = "[Scope.GetState]"
						blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
							block "rival_tooltip" {}
						}
						blockoverride "row_lo" {
							block "rival_lo" {}
						}
						blockoverride "row_hi" {
							block "rival_hi" {}
						}
						blockoverride "row_est" {
							block "rival_est" {}
						}
						blockoverride "row_range" {
							block "rival_range" {}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Program Effects: the modifiers the milestone's entry puts on the country,
	### which the journal window draws in its header and a tab otherwise shows
	### in te_je_modifier_strip (gui/te_system_tab_widgets.gui): the same two
	### datamodels, grouped under a ruled subheading (2026-11-24 evaluation:
	### about thirty icons with no heading read as part of the Program row).
	### Ongoing: JournalEntry.GetScalingModifiers, the entry's
	### scaling_modifiers_while_active (cost, funding, approach, choices, and
	### solar colonization's worlds, facilities and colonies), 35 px icons, 12 to
	### a row (12 x 35 + 11 x 5 = 475), left-aligned so a short last row sits
	### under the one above. Timed: JournalEntry.GetTimedModifiers (the safety
	### review after a setback), one row each: icon, name and time left, 25 + 269
	### + 170 + 2 x 8 = 480. The engine gives the two lists and no finer kind, so
	### there are two groups. Each group, and the panel, draws only with
	### something in it. The Timeline Extended window's milestone frames draw it
	### under the entry's datacontext, in the player's own part
	### (gen_te_systems_window._milestone); te_own_country_only as the shared
	### strip has it, since it reads JournalEntry (gotcha #35).
	type te_sr_program_effects = flowcontainer {
		using = te_own_country_only
		parentanchor = hcenter
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		te_sr_panel = {
			visible = "[Or( Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetScalingModifiers ) ), Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetTimedModifiers ) ) )]"
			spacing = 4

			te_sr_subheader = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_effects_header_tt"
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_effects_header"
				}
			}

			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetScalingModifiers ) )]"
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }

				textbox = {
					autoresize = yes
					maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = te_sr_fontsize_row
					default_format = "#title"
					text = "je_space_race_widget_effects_ongoing"
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_effects_ongoing_tt"
				}
				flowcontainer = {
					spacing = 5
					wrap_count = 12
					datamodel = "[JournalEntry.GetScalingModifiers]"

					item = {
						icon = {
							size = { 35 35 }
							using = tooltip_se
							tooltip = "[ScalingModifier.GetTooltip]"
							texture = "[ScalingModifier.GetIcon]"
						}
					}
				}
			}

			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetTimedModifiers ) )]"
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }

				textbox = {
					autoresize = yes
					maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = te_sr_fontsize_row
					default_format = "#title"
					text = "je_space_race_widget_effects_timed"
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_effects_timed_tt"
				}
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = vertical
					spacing = 4
					datamodel = "[JournalEntry.GetTimedModifiers]"

					item = {
						flowcontainer = {
							direction = horizontal
							spacing = 8
							tooltip = "[TimedModifier.GetTooltip]"
							using = tooltip_se

							icon = {
								size = { 25 25 }
								parentanchor = vcenter
								texture = "[TimedModifier.GetIcon]"
							}
							textbox = {
								autoresize = yes
								multiline = yes
								minimumsize = { 269 -1 }
								maximumsize = { 269 -1 }
								parentanchor = vcenter
								align = left|nobaseline
								using = te_sr_fontsize_row
								text = "[TimedModifier.GetName]"
							}
							textbox = {
								autoresize = yes
								multiline = yes
								minimumsize = { 170 -1 }
								maximumsize = { 170 -1 }
								parentanchor = vcenter
								align = right|nobaseline
								using = te_sr_fontsize_row
								default_format = "#v"
								text = "[TimedModifier.GetRemainingDuration]"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### One colony in Colonies (audit SPC-5; the colony sections of slices 2-6 in
	### one table), in its own framed box (colony management design § 8): its
	### icon and name on the first line, the name a button (its hover its
	### specializations' effects, a click the colony's window) with vanilla's
	### go-to arrow beside it (the owner, 2026-10-30); beside them the chosen view's status
	### and buttons, and under it the view's figures. The views (te_sr_sec_colonies'
	### switch, GetVariableSystem's sr_colony_view): People, the default (the
	### settlers' priority; people / room, crews), Modules (Clear; the crews'
	### share, slots and Extraplanetary Base room, then every module type in three
	### lines of self-labeled cells, te_sr_mod_cell), Autonomy (charter or garrison, and
	### Abandon; autonomy, its drift a month and what the colony is building
	### itself) and, under Full Colonies, Defenses (status; Defenses, integrity,
	### marines). A colony's page is a type of its own, te_sr_colony_page, in
	### the Colonies window (te_sr_colony_popup, the owner 2026-11-23), filled
	### from the same blocks as this row; the name and the arrow open the
	### window on this colony (colony_focus: sr_colony_focus its key, te_popup
	### sr_colony). Under Races Only the row is the first line's icon and name,
	### plain text: there is nothing to manage, so no window. Line 1: 24 + 180 + 24 + the widest
	### view's part (Autonomy's 80 + 80 + 4) + 3 x 4 + 2 x 4 margin = 412; the
	### module cells 4 + 5 x 90 + 4 x 4 + 8 = 478, in the 480 column. Instances in te_sr_colony_rows
	### (sr_sites_generated_rows.gui), one per world.
	type te_sr_colony_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		margin = { 4 3 }
		block "colony_visible" {}

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_simple
		}

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4

			widget = {
				size = { 24 24 }
				parentanchor = top

				icon = {
					size = { 24 24 }
					parentanchor = center
					block "colony_icon" {}
				}
			}
			### The name: a click opens the colony's window (colony management design § 8).
			### It reads as a button (vanilla's clean_button, as the countries list's
			### names), with vanilla's go-to arrow beside it (the owner, 2026-10-30).
			button = {
				visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				size = { 180 24 }
				parentanchor = top
				using = clean_button
				block "colony_focus" {}

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = left|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 180
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = te_sr_fontsize_row
					elide = right
					block "colony_name" {}
				}
			}
			### Races Only: the name alone, its hover the specializations' effects.
			widget = {
				visible = "[Not( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				size = { 180 24 }
				parentanchor = top

				textbox = {
					parentanchor = left|vcenter
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 180
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = te_sr_fontsize_row
					elide = right
					block "colony_name" {}
				}
			}
			button_icon_goto = {
				visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				size = { 24 24 }
				parentanchor = top
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_colony_open_tt"
				block "colony_focus" {}
			}
			### The view parts: one in a list, every one stacked on a colony's page.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 1

				### People: the colony's priority for settlers (sr_colony_priority_sgui).
				button = {
					visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), Not( Or( GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'modules'), Or( GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'autonomy'), Or( And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_full'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'defences') ), And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_ebase_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'bases') ) ) ) ) ) )]"
					using = default_button_action
					size = { 80 24 }
					block "priority_button" {}

					textbox = {
						parentanchor = center
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 74
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						text = "je_space_race_widget_emig_prio_0"
						block "prio_0_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = center
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 74
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						text = "je_space_race_widget_emig_prio_1"
						block "prio_1_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = center
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 74
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						text = "je_space_race_widget_emig_prio_2"
						block "prio_2_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = center
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 74
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						text = "je_space_race_widget_emig_prio_3"
						block "prio_3_visible" {}
					}
				}
				### Modules: Clear, which empties the colony's queue.
				flowcontainer = {
					visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'modules') )]"
					direction = horizontal
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					spacing = 4

					button_icon_cancel = {
						size = { 24 24 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						block "module_clear_button" {}
					}
				}
				### Autonomy: its charter or garrison, and Abandon (sr_colony_abandon_sgui).
				flowcontainer = {
					visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_contested'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'autonomy') )]"
					direction = horizontal
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					spacing = 4
					parentanchor = vcenter

					widget = {
						size = { 80 24 }
						parentanchor = vcenter

						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 80
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							default_format = "#grey"
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_status_none"
							block "aut_none_visible" {}
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 80
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_charter_tt"
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_status_charter"
							block "aut_charter_visible" {}
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 80
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_garrison_tt"
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_status_garrison"
							block "aut_garrison_visible" {}
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 80
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_both_tt"
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_status_both"
							block "aut_both_visible" {}
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 80
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_status_held"
							block "aut_held_visible" {}
						}
					}
					button = {
						using = default_button_action
						size = { 80 24 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						block "aut_abandon_button" {}

						textbox = {
							parentanchor = center
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 74
							align = center|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							text = "je_space_race_widget_autonomy_abandon"
						}
					}
				}
				### Defenses (Full Colonies): calm, blockaded, under assault, occupied
				### (with the occupier's flag) or interdicted.
				widget = {
					visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_colonies_full'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('sr_colony_view', 'defences') )]"
					size = { 140 24 }
					parentanchor = vcenter

					textbox = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 140
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						default_format = "#grey"
						text = "je_space_race_widget_def_status_calm"
						block "def_calm_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 140
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_loc_blockaded_tt"
						text = "je_space_race_widget_def_status_blockaded"
						block "def_blockaded_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 140
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_loc_interdicted_tt"
						text = "je_space_race_widget_def_status_interdicted"
						block "def_interdicted_visible" {}
					}
					textbox = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 140
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = te_sr_fontsize_row
						elide = right
						tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_def_assault_tt"
						text = "je_space_race_widget_def_status_assault"
						block "def_assault_visible" {}
					}
					flowcontainer = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						direction = horizontal
						spacing = 4
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						block "def_occupied_visible" {}

						textbox = {
							parentanchor = vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 100
							align = left|nobaseline
							using = te_sr_fontsize_row
							elide = right
							tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_def_occupied_tt"
							text = "je_space_race_widget_def_status_occupied"
						}
						flowcontainer = {
